        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(a) An Employee's Term of Employment will be broken if the Employee falls to return to work on or before the day following the expiration date of such a Leave of Absence except in case prior arrangements for extension have been completed. Such Leaves of Absence may be terminated prior to the expiration date if the Employee gives the Manager ten (10) days prior written notice of intention to return to work and returns to work on the date specified. Notice of intention to return to work of a Union Representative shall include assurance that the provisions of Paragraph 5(a)(1), above, will be met as described in Paragraph 5(c), above.",
